    "sourceWikitext": "__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Hungarian recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Hungary|Cuisine of Hungary]] | [[Cookbook:Vegetarian cuisine|Vegetarian cuisine]]\n\n'''Kovaim''' are Hungarian cheese [[Cookbook:Dumpling|dumplings]]. They go well with [[Cookbook:Cheddar Cheese|cheddar cheese]] and [[Cookbook:Ketchup|ketchup]].\n\n==Ingredients==\n===Dough===\n*300 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n*3 large [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]s\n*½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n\n===Filling===\n*Dry [[Cookbook:Ricotta|ricotta cheese]]\n*Salt to taste\n\n==Procedure==\n# Mix the flour, salt, eggs and water into a [[Cookbook:Dough|dough]]. [[Cookbook:Kneading|Knead]] it until it is very smooth.\n# Cover the dough in a plastic bowl, and let it rest for at least half an hour.\n# Combine the ricotta and salt to make the filling.\n# [[Cookbook:Dough#Rolling|Roll]] the dough out into a sheet as thin as possible (about 3 [[Cookbook:Mm|mm]] thick). Cut into squares, and fill each square with some filling. Fold the dough over the filling diagonally to make a triangular dumpling.\n# [[Cookbook:Boiling|Boil]] the dumplings in water for about 5 minutes.\n# Serve hot.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* You can also fill these dumplings with cooked [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]] and [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]], or ricotta cheese with sugar for a sweet dumpling.\n* You could add some spicier cheese to the filling like cheddar, or even Parmesan, but make sure this is not more than a third of the filling.\n\n[[Category:Hungarian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ricotta]]\n[[Category:Dumpling recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]",
